From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] powrprof: the legacy numbered power scheme API

- EnumPwrSchemes, ReadPwrScheme, WritePwrScheme, DeletePwrScheme,
  GetActivePwrScheme, SetActivePwrScheme, ReadGlobalPwrPolicy,
  WriteGlobalPwrPolicy, ReadProcessorPwrScheme, WriteProcessorPwrScheme and
  GetCurrentPowerPolicies were stubs returning ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED or
  doing nothing. They now work, in a new powrprof/legacy.c, over schemes
  numbered like Windows does: 0 to 5 (Home/Office Desk ... Max Battery) are
  always there with policies derived from the GUID scheme each stands for
  (balanced, high performance, power saver, so both APIs agree) and new
  schemes (WritePwrScheme with NEWSCHEME, now defined) get ids from 6 that are
  never reused. What a program writes is kept under
  HKCU\Control Panel\PowerCfg.
- EnumPwrSchemes passes name and description sizes in bytes including the NUL,
  in id order, and stops when the callback returns FALSE.
- SetActivePwrScheme also switches the GUID scheme (PowerSetActiveScheme), and
  GetActivePwrScheme follows a later PowerSetActiveScheme instead of
  reporting the stale number. The active scheme cannot be deleted
  (ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED); unknown ids give ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND and NULL
  pointers ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER.

Gate: test/powerlegacy-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, fresh profile each,
test/powerlegacy-probe.c). Mutants SG_MUTANT_LPW_NEWID/ENUM_STOP/NAMESIZE/
DELETE_ACTIVE/ACTIVE_STALE (powrprof/legacy.c).
---
--- a/dlls/powrprof/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/powrprof/Makefile.in
@@ -3,5 +3,6 @@ IMPORTLIB = powrprof
 IMPORTS   = advapi32 user32 rpcrt4
 
 SOURCES = \
+	legacy.c \
 	powrprof.c \
 	schemes.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/powrprof/legacy.c
@@ -0,0 +1,709 @@
+/*
+ * The legacy (pre-Vista) power scheme API: numbered schemes with a name,
+ * a description and a POWER_POLICY, one global policy, and a processor
+ * policy per scheme.
+ *
+ * Copyright 2026 Stained Glass OS
+ *
